# PRD Validation Checklist

> Use for the **validate** intent. Grade each item PASS / CONCERN / FAIL and tie
> every finding to a PRD section. Report; do not rewrite.

## Decision-readiness
- [ ] A reader could decide go/no-go from this PRD alone.
- [ ] The MVP cut is real — something meaningful is out of scope.
- [ ] Non-Goals are explicit and non-empty.

## Substance
- [ ] Every feature has ≥1 numbered functional requirement (`FR-N`).
- [ ] Every `FR-N` is behavioral and testable (can become an EARS requirement).
- [ ] Each key journey is concrete (named persona, real beats), not abstract.

## Coherence
- [ ] Glossary terms are used identically throughout — no synonym drift.
- [ ] Features trace back to a user job; no orphan features.
- [ ] Success metrics reference the `FR-N`(s) they measure.
- [ ] At least one counter-metric exists.

## Honesty
- [ ] Every unverified claim is marked `[ASSUMPTION]` and listed in the index.
- [ ] Open questions are captured, not hidden.
- [ ] No solution/architecture detail has leaked into the "what/why".

## Findings
| Section | Severity | Finding | Suggested direction |
